# ===========================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT backend.tf — this file does not end in .tf and Terraform
# does not read it. Renaming it without reading the reason below is a mistake.
# ===========================================================================
#
# GLM-001 M3.3 is BLOCKED on M1.6, and blocked in a specific way.
#
# --- Why this is not just "waiting for the bank to name a backend" ----------
#
# SEC-F07 / IMP-15 / RISK-027, raised by Board 4 on 2026-08-29:
#
#   GitLab-managed Terraform state is available in Free/CE on self-managed, and
#   is the attractive answer to M1.6. For delivery/infrastructure state it is
#   fine. For THIS state it is structurally wrong.
#
#   This state controls the estate's groups and projects. Stored inside that
#   estate, an apply that damages the estate ALSO damages its own state, and
#   recovery requires the thing that was just destroyed.
#
#   It satisfies none of C-SEC-6's three requirements:
#     - separate backend   -> same instance
#     - separate KMS key   -> instance-managed encryption
#     - distinct identity  -> the same automation account
#
# --- What goes here when M1.6 resolves --------------------------------------
#
# A backend OUTSIDE the GitLab instance. The enterprise S3/KMS platform if that
# is the bank standard, or an approved equivalent. Requirements from baseline
# section 4.4, all mandatory:
#
#   encryption at rest | access restricted to SRE/platform operators
#   state locking      | versioning and history
#   documented AND TESTED recovery   <- untested restore is a belief, not a control
#   never in git
#
# Illustrative shape only — do not uncomment, the values are placeholders:
#
#   terraform {
#     backend "s3" {
#       bucket         = "<bank-approved-bucket>"
#       key            = "gitlab-bootstrap/terraform.tfstate"
#       region         = "ap-south-1"          # residency: C-CMP-1 applies here too
#       encrypt        = true
#       kms_key_id     = "<bootstrap-specific-key-not-shared-with-app-state>"
#       dynamodb_table = "<lock-table>"
#     }
#   }
#
# Note the residency point: this state describes the whole estate, so ASM-022
# and C-CMP-1 apply to where the state itself lives, not only to GitLab.
#
# Until then, no apply runs. Local state is prohibited and there is no fallback.
